  "body": "## Request\n\nTo drive CamCraft from an agent today, a user installs the full application. An install-free MCP server (`uvx camcraft mcp` or `pipx run camcraft mcp`) would let any agent use CamCraft headless.\n\n## Proposal (needs design)\n\nPublish the headless `camcraft-cli` as a Python wheel per platform (the binary inside the wheel), with the entry point `camcraft mcp`. Open questions: wheel size, the platforms (macOS universal, Linux x86_64 and aarch64, Windows x86_64), signing, and the release step in `release.yml` (billed minutes).\n\nDone means: a design decision in `docs/decisions/` and the sub-issues for the work.\n\nIdea from SolidCraft 0.51 (`uvx solidcraft mcp`); our own implementation.\n",
